    "reason": "Over the last 30 days this campaign had a steady ROAS of 4.0 ($50 spend and $200 revenue per day) and a CPA of $25. That is clearly stronger than example-b. However, it spends only $50 a day against a $100 cap, so the budget is not what limits it. Raising the cap would likely not increase spend, and the cause is more likely audience size, bids or creative. Keep the budget at $100 and look at delivery limits such as bid strategy, audience and creative. If spend starts reaching the cap, raise the budget by no more than 20% at a time. The campaign is still flagged as 'learning', and at about 2 conversions a day (roughly 14 a week) it may not reach the usual ~50 a week needed to exit. Bigger budget jumps could reset learning. The data also ends 2026-09-30, so Oct 1 is not reflected."
